  "result": "I graded s1 and wrote `grades/0001-s1.json`: q1 and q3 correct, q5 and q6 partial, q2 and q4 wrong.\n\n- **q2 and q4 (wrong, M4):** you treated the model as running the tools itself. The model only outputs a tool request, and the program runs the tool. In q4 that makes 3 tool requests plus the final answer, so 4 calls.\n- **q5 (partial):** \"Sends it back to the model\" is the what. The why is missing: the model needs the result to choose its next step or write the answer.\n- **q6 (partial, M3):** picking a tool from the names and descriptions it is sent is right. The model does not remember past sessions on its own; any memory is the program resending text.\n\n**Pattern:** you give the model jobs that belong to the program, namely running tools and remembering.\n\n**Next step:** redraw your laser cutter trace as two columns, model and program, and mark which side does each step.\n\nThe `grade-reviewer` returned KEEP with only minor findings, and I applied those wording fixes. I also added `review-records/0001-s1-grade.md`, `learning-records/0003-model-vs-program-roles.md` and the `NOTES.md` update. s2 is still ungraded.",
